FROM qwen3-4b-deforum-dual-stream-lora:v1

# Qwen3-4B video dual-stream prompt model (QLoRA, merged to Q8 GGUF).
# Trained on the RAW "### Instruction / ### Response" text format — NOT a chat
# template. Routing is by a dialect prefix inside the user message; the prefix IS
# the routing signal and must vary, so there is no single auto-prefix:
#   "Generate a WanVideo (UMT5) prompt for: <concept>"
#   "Generate an LTX-Video prompt for: <concept>"
#   "Write a compact video caption for: <concept>"
#
# The TEMPLATE wraps the user prompt in the training scaffold, so callers
# (ComfyUI, CLI) send only "<dialect prefix> <concept>" and still get clean,
# preamble-free output. Without this wrapper a bare prefix leaks a markdown
# header ("### WanVideo Prompt: ...") — the FC failure mode found in validation.
TEMPLATE """### Instruction:
{{ .Prompt }}

### Response:
"""

PARAMETER temperature 0.7
PARAMETER top_p 0.9
PARAMETER repeat_penalty 1.2
PARAMETER num_ctx 4096
PARAMETER stop "### Instruction:"
